  "recommendation": "Report ASR_rel alongside the raw subgroup FNR shift and the clean model's sensitivity at the same operating point. Do not compare ASR_rel across cohorts or thresholds whose clean sensitivities differ without stating the inflation factor.",
  "headline_sentence": "ASR_rel divides the raw increase in missed positives by the clean model's sensitivity at the chosen operating point, so it inflates that increase by a factor of 1/sensitivity: across the cohorts and operating points reported here that factor ranges from 1.05 (clean sensitivity 0.96) to 8.36 (clean sensitivity 0.13), which is why the same attack can appear to install at a fourfold lower poison rate when it is read at a threshold no deployed system would use."
